   "Flow model: at Re = 9.24×10^6 a laminar boundary layer is about 0.0016 vehicle lengths thick, i.e. 0.3 cells -- too thin for this grid -- so a WALE large-eddy model represents the unresolved scales and third-order upwind advection keeps the run stable.",
   "Reading the numbers: this is a 2D side profile, an infinitely wide car. Air cannot escape around the sides, so the flow over the roof is faster, the wake sheds as a 2D vortex street and the underbody is a channel; Cd and Cl (per frontal height) therefore come out well above 3D wind-tunnel values. The sedan template on a moving road gives Cd ≈ 0.6 and Cl ≈ 2.5-2.8 at Draft and 0.72 and 2.2 at Standard, where a real saloon measures about 0.3 and 0.1-0.4. The quality preset itself moves the numbers by 20-25 % (resolution, underbody cells, blockage), so rank and compare designs simulated at the same quality; do not quote them as absolute values.",
   "Duration: 30 convective times L/U (4.50 s of real flow); forces are averaged from t = 6 (or later, where the start-up transient is found to end), and the run stops early once the mean drag is known to ±5 % and the mean lift to ±10 % (one standard error) and neither drifts.",
   "Time step ≈ 0.00079 L/U from the stability limit (CFL 0.5): about 37,964 steps, estimated 2 min 12 s on GPU · NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Ti (8.0 GB).",
